  "description": "The fatal close - the third and last abend site, and the only one that is reached after the loop has run to completion. All three records are read and displayed twice each, the browse reaches '10' and sets END-OF-FILE, and then CLOSE at app/cbl/CBCUS01C.cbl:L138 reports '42'. 9000-CUSTFILE-CLOSE expresses its guard arithmetically - ADD 8 TO ZERO GIVING APPL-RESULT before the close, SUBTRACT APPL-RESULT FROM APPL-RESULT on success, ADD 12 TO ZERO GIVING APPL-RESULT otherwise - and reaches the same three values the open reaches by MOVE. The ELSE arm at L147-L150 displays 'ERROR CLOSING CUSTOMER FILE', the status through the numeric branch as FILE STATUS IS: NNNN0042, and 'ABENDING PROGRAM'. The L85 banner is never emitted, which is the difference between this and a clean run: the records are all there and the closing banner is not.",
